 "caveat": "\u26a0 A pin is an explorer's word on a date, not a node. It is recorded so a reader can recompute it against the chain, which is the only thing that settles it. Each block below names the operators that AGREED on its hash and merkle root; at least 2 must agree or nothing is pinned, and any disagreement is a refusal rather than a vote. Note the independence is partial and deliberately stated: blockstream and mempool are different operators running the same Esplora software, blockchain.info is a different codebase. Agreement across them is harder to forge than one API and is not the same thing as running your own node.",
